  "facts": [
    "O'Connell Bridge, originally Carlisle Bridge, was designed by James Gandon and built between 1791 and 1794 as a humped, granite arch structure with Portland stone balustrades and corner obelisks.",
    "Between 1877 and 1880, the bridge was widened to 50 m (160 ft) wide, reopened in 1882, and renamed after Daniel O'Connell, whose statue now graces the central island.",
    "In 2004 pranksters installed a hidden plaque honoring Father Pat Noise, which remained unnoticed until 2006 and was still visible as of June 2020."
